## Context

The JETP programme (Just Energy Transition Partnerships, with Christophe
Cassen, CIRED) now counts three papers in progress plus a historical deposit
(hal-04412457, 2024). It lived autonomously, moved on 2026-09-10 from
`~/CNRS/papiers/actif/JETP at two/` to `~/CNRS/projets/actifs/jetp/` (a plain
`mv`, not yet reorganised according to this repository's conventions). The
author decided today: JETP becomes a stratum of `climate-finance-het` rather
than an independent project.

**Why.** Both programmes measure climate finance on OECD CRS data. The short
JETP paper (macro mechanism, disbursement reference curve) and paper 3
(ledger) build their own CRS/IATI pull pipeline (`analyse-crs/pull_crs.py`,
`pilote-ledger-vn/iati-crs/`, ~322 MB of raw pulls) which presumably overlaps
the CRS infrastructure already present here (`data/book/riomarkers/`,
`config/corpus_filter.yaml`, DVC pipeline with padme as data authority).
Merging avoids maintaining two CRS pipelines and lets the JETP measurement
papers cite/reuse an already verified corpus-building machinery.

**What stays out of scope**, explicitly (see Invariants): paper 1 (2024
deposit) and the AFD-Senegal file with R. Blachier, paused on 2026-09-10
(`enquete-afd-senelec-2026-09-09.md`, central figure EUR 670 M unverified).

